    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0514" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg480"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr.
                            Barrett.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 138.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatches Nos. 221 and 222, both dated the 22dof July last, and relating to the
                    arbitration of the Cheek case.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to inform you that the postponement of the date of the
                    arbitration of said case to February 1 next is acceptable to the Department.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
